To bring the exact same filtering functionality and permanently visible 3-dot menus to your Authorization page, you will need to make the matching updates in **VoucherAuthorization.js**.
Here are the exact replacements needed for that file:
### 1. Update the Import
At the top of VoucherAuthorization.js, update your DataGrid import to include GridToolbar.
**Replace this:**
```javascript
import { DataGrid } from "@mui/x-data-grid";

```
**With this:**
```javascript
import { DataGrid, GridToolbar } from "@mui/x-data-grid";

```
### 2. Update the Styles (Always Visible 3 Dots)
Find the styles object near the top of the file, specifically the dataGridContainer, and add the overrides.
**Replace the dataGridContainer block with this:**
```javascript
  dataGridContainer: {
    height: 600,
    width: "100%",
    backgroundColor: "background.paper",
    boxShadow: 2,
    borderRadius: 2,
    border: 1,
    borderColor: "divider",
    "& .MuiDataGrid-columnHeaders": {
      backgroundColor: (theme) => alpha(theme.palette.primary.main, 0.08),
      fontWeight: "bold",
      fontSize: "0.95rem",
    },
    "& .MuiDataGrid-row:hover": {
      backgroundColor: (theme) => alpha(theme.palette.primary.main, 0.04),
    },
    // --- ADD THESE TWO BLOCKS TO KEEP THE 3 DOTS ALWAYS VISIBLE ---
    "& .MuiDataGrid-menuIcon": {
      visibility: "visible !important",
      width: "auto !important",
    },
    "& .MuiDataGrid-iconButtonContainer": {
      visibility: "visible !important",
      width: "auto !important",
    },
  },

```
