```
*(Make sure to explicitly add filterable: false to the workflowState, creatorName, requestDate, requestCount, and actions column definitions as well, so the filter dropdown doesn't get cluttered with unsupported columns).*
### 4. Update the DataGrid Component
Finally, inject the GridToolbar into the DataGrid near the bottom of the file.
**Find your <DataGrid> component and update the slots and slotProps like this:**
```javascript
        <DataGrid
          rows={rows}
          columns={columns}
          loading={loading}
          getRowId={(row) => row.batchId}
          disableRowSelectionOnClick
          pageSizeOptions={[5, 10, 25]}
          disableColumnResize
          rowHeight={52}
          initialState={{
            pagination: { paginationModel: { page: 0, pageSize: 10 } },
          }}
          
          // --- UPDATE THESE TWO PROPS ---
          slots={{ 
            noRowsOverlay: CustomNoRowsOverlay,
            toolbar: GridToolbar // <--- Adds the inbuilt filter toolbar
          }}
          slotProps={{
            toolbar: {
              printOptions: { disableToolbarButton: true },
              csvOptions: { disableToolbarButton: true },
              showQuickFilter: false,
            }
          }}
          
          sx={styles.dataGridContainer}
        />

```
This will perfectly mirror the behavior you just set up on the Status screen, keeping the UI completely consistent!
